'use client';
/**
 * C9_MathsProbabilitySim (Class 9 Maths)
 *
 * ONE chapter: Probability -- the experimental approach (NCERT IX).
 * Two honest ideas, both computed live:
 *   Empirical P(E)  = (times E happened) / (total trials)      -- measured
 *   Theoretical P(E)= (favourable outcomes) / (total outcomes) -- reasoned
 * Trials are generated by a SEEDED linear congruential generator, so a
 * given seed + click sequence always yields the SAME data: deterministic,
 * reproducible, no Math.random at render time. The Law of Large Numbers
 * panel compares |empirical − theoretical| with its 1/√N envelope.
 *
 * Deep layout (5 tabs):
 *   1. Predict    -- guess before rolling
 *   2. Dice Lab   -- roll, tally, compare with theory
 *   3. Trend Lab  -- running difference vs the 1/√N envelope
 *   4. Challenge  -- 9 questions in 3 tiers with hints
 *   5. Truths     -- misconception killer + honest summary
 */
